  "body": "## Why\n\nSix releases landed in one day — the window, the window picker, nine settings, persistence, and a Windows installer fix — and **none of it was in the user-facing docs**. Anyone reading the README would not know `mcc-desktop` had a window at all.\n\n## What was written, and where\n\n- **README** — a `## Desktop App` section: the three server modes (`spawn`/`attach`/`off`), the window provider chain, `--window`, the opt-in `--desktop` installer flag, and the nine `DESKTOP_*` settings by name.\n- **docs/USAGE.md** — five anchored, task-shaped subsections plus two Troubleshooting entries pointing back at the two gotchas most likely to be hit.\n- **The in-dashboard Guide** — extends the existing deployment section. Documentation belongs where the user is, and they read the dashboard.\n- **docs/BRAND.md** — checked, left alone; the icon table is already accurate.\n\n## The awkward facts are stated, not smoothed over\n\nEach of these is a question somebody will otherwise ask:\n\n> app-mode is the default because three things the dashboard depends on break inside an embedded webview: `window.open` (both OAuth logins), `<a download>` (the analytics export), and `navigator.clipboard` (every copy button).\n\n- **pywebview ships disabled**, with the reason given rather than hidden.\n- **`DESKTOP_*` settings apply on the NEXT launch**, not to a running tray — a setting that appears to do nothing is worse than one that is absent.\n- **WSL and headless have no tray**; `mcc-server` is the path, reached from a browser on the Windows side.\n- **`--desktop` is opt-in**; a default install creates no shortcuts.\n\n## Verification\n\n**Full suite: 6 failed, 4377 passed, 26 skipped** — the same six PowerShell installer failures, zero new.\n\n**`tests/contracts/`: 192 passed**, which matters more than usual here. The asset-wiring guards added earlier this arc mean any class added to `index.html` without a CSS rule now fails the suite — so the Guide edit reuses the existing `guide-note` / `guide-note-warn` classes rather than inventing any.\n\nEvery pre-existing README anchor is intact (one new `desktop-app` anchor added); the diff is **174 insertions and no deletions**. The provider table was not touched.\n\n## Version bump\n\n`index.html` lives under `src/my_claude_code/api/`, which this project's versioning rules count as production even for a text-only change. Hence 5.30.2 rather than no bump.\n\n## Residual risk\n\n**The Guide was not rendered in a browser.** The markup was checked mechanically — every class resolves to a real rule, every anchor to a real id — which is the cheap substitute, not a substitute for looking.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
